lego:evidence  a  owl:AnnotationProperty .

:R-HSA-6803204  a           owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Apoptotic transcriptional targets of TP53 include genes that regulate the permeability of the mitochondrial membrane and/or cytochrome C release, such as BAX, BID, PMAIP1 (NOXA), BBC3 (PUMA) and probably BNIP3L, AIFM2, STEAP3, TRIAP1 and TP53AIP1 (Miyashita and Reed 1995, Oda et al. 2000, Samuels-Lev et al. 2001, Nakano and Vousden 2001, Sax et al. 2002, Passer et al. 2003, Bergamaschi et al. 2004, Li et al. 2004, Fei et al. 2004, Wu et al. 2004, Park and Nakamura 2005, Patel et al. 2008, Wang et al. 2012, Wilson et al. 2013), thus promoting the activation of the apoptotic pathway.<p>Transcriptional activation of TP53AIP1 requires phosphorylation of TP53 at serine residue S46 (Oda et al. 2000, Taira et al. 2007). Phosphorylation of TP53 at S46 is regulated by another TP53 pro-apoptotic target, TP53INP1 (Okamura et al. 2001, Tomasini et al. 2003)." ;
        rdfs:label          "TP53 Regulates Transcription of Genes Involved in Cytochrome C Release" ;
        dc:contributor      "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Authored: Orlic-Milacic, Marija, 2015-10-14" , "Reviewed: Inga, Alberto, 2016-02-04" , "Edited: Orlic-Milacic, Marija, 2015-10-14" , "Reviewed: Zaccara, Sara, 2016-02-04" ;
        dc:date             "2026-07-02" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-6803204" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-5633008/R-HSA-5633008> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

